    "text": "<p>Consider the reaction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>KCl</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>NOCl</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>KNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>The amount of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> required to produce<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>110</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is</p><p>(Given : Atomic masses of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>39</mn></math>, respectively.)</p>",
